According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Modular Green Wall Systems market was valued at USD 1.40 billion in 2024 and is projected to grow from USD 1.50 billion in 2025 to USD 2.28 billion by 2031, registering a CAGR of 7.4% during the forecast period. The market is being propelled by rapid urbanization, increasing adoption of sustainable building practices, stringent environmental regulations, rising awareness of biophilic design, and growing demand for energy-efficient and aesthetically appealing building solutions.
Modular green wall systems, also known as vertical gardens or living walls, are engineered structures designed to support vegetation on vertical surfaces. These systems typically consist of modular panels, preserved or synthetic vegetation, irrigation mechanisms, and structural frameworks that enable relatively flexible installation and maintenance. The technology is increasingly being incorporated into commercial buildings, residential developments, hospitality venues, retail spaces, healthcare facilities, educational institutions, and smart city projects.
